    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0609" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/688</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Commerce</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-11">August 11, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dean</hi>: Your letter of the 1st, file TA
                    611.2531/681, has had consideration.</p>
                <pb facs="0610" n="600" xml:id="pg600"/>
                <p>The matter of an excise tax on copper from Chile or the amount of such excise tax
                    is one for the President and the Secretary to determine. There probably should
                    be some excise tax, although 4 cents appears quite high.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad to discuss the matter further if you wish.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jesse H. Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
